                "code": "Example\nint isLoggedIn = 1;\nint isAdmin = 0;\n\nprintf(\"Regular user: %d\\n\", isLoggedIn && !isAdmin);\nprintf(\"Has access: %d\\n\", isLoggedIn || isAdmin);\nprintf(\"Not logged in: %d\\n\", !isLoggedIn);\n\nResult:\n\n Regular user: 1\n\n Has access: 1\n\n Not logged in: 0\n\nTry it Yourself »\n\n Remember: in C, 1 means true and 0 means false. Logical operators often become easier to understand once you start using them inside if statements, which you will learn about in the upcoming chapters.\n\nAdvertisement\n -->\n\n❮ Previous\nNext ❯\n\n that follows an inside #main (tutorial lessons; this skips the\n hero/cert cards at the top of landing pages).\n Buttons: X / Facebook / LinkedIn / Copy link. Shares the page URL + title. -->\n\n ★\n\n +1\n\n Sign in to track progress",
